			<!-- Begin Content Area -->
<p class="pageheads">Important Information About GAIN and GAIN-Supported Software</p>
<!-- begin content -->

<style>
	#logo-box
	{
		background-color: #D7D7D7;
		border: 1px solid #868686;
		width: 135px;
	}
	#logo-box li
	{
		font-size: 12px;
	}
	
	#logo-box img 
	{
		margin-bottom: 1em;
	}
</style>
<div id="logo-box" style="background-image: url(logo-list-bg.gif); background-repeat: repeat-x;  float: right; margin: 0 0 2em 2em; padding: 1.5em; text-align: center;">
	<h4>List of GAIN-Supported Software:</h4>
	<ul style="list-style-type: none; margin: 0; padding: 0;">
		<li>
			<img alt="DashBar logo" src="logo-dashbar-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="Date Manager logo" src="logo-date-manager-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="EntryPass logo" src="logo-entrypass-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="Gator eWallet logo" src="logo-gator-ewallet-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="GotSmiley logo" src="logo-gotsmiley-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="Offer Companion logo" src="logo-offer-companion-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="Precision Time logo" src="logo-precision-time-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="ScreenScenes logo" src="logo-screenscenes-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="Weatherscope logo" src="logo-weatherscope-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
		<li>
			<img alt="WebSecureAlert logo" src="logo-websecurealert-90x30.gif" />
		</li>
	</ul>
	<ul style="border-top: 1px solid #868686; list-style-type: none; margin: 2em 0 0 0; padding: 2em 0 0 0;">
		<li>DashBar</li>
		<li>Date Manager</li>
		<li>EntryPass</li>
		<li>Gator eWallet</li>
		<li>GotSmiley</li>
		<li>Offer Companion</li>
		<li>Precision Time</li>
		<li>ScreenScenes</li>
		<li>Weatherscope</li>
		<li>WebSecureAlert</li>
	</ul>
</div><p>You were redirected to this page if you clicked on a link related to GAIN-supported software.</p>
<p>Claria Corporation is no longer supporting GAIN-Supported software.  If you have GAIN-Supported Software installed on your computer, it may not continue to function properly. We therefore recommend that you remove any GAIN-Supported Software you may have on your computer.</p>
<p>A list of all GAIN Supported Software is posted on this Web page.  Please compare the software listed in your programs list (Start/Programs) to this list.  Should you recognize any of the software on the list, you should uninstall it now using the Add/Remove Programs feature in the Control Panel.</p>
<p>Claria Corporation, which formerly distributed GAIN software, has shut down the GAIN Network.  This means that Claria stopped sending GAIN pop-up and other advertisements to your computer via the GAIN Network, and no longer collects anonymous information from your computer via the GAIN Network about your Web surfing and computer use.  If you used a GAIN-Supported software program before October 1, 2006, we may continue to use this previously collected anonymous information in the aggregate to:</p>
<ol> 
	<li>Conduct research for use in developing new products and to compile analytics and custom marketing research programs to better understand how consumers use the web.</li>
	<li>Develop reports for our corporate clients using aggregated, anonymous information so that they can understand trends in online consumer behavior.</li>
</ol>
<p>Our server may contact your computer and uninstall two files from your computer, called GMT.exe and CMESys.exe as part of the process to shut down the GAIN network.  This uninstall will not negatively affect your computer or GAIN-supported software on your computer.</p>
<h3>Helpful Information:</h3>
<h4>How to uninstall GAIN-Supported software:</h4>
<ol>
	<li>From the Windows Start button, select "Settings", and then "Control Panel".</li> 
	<li>When the Control Panel window opens, double-click on the "Add/Remove Programs" icon.</li> 
	<li>When the Add/Remove Programs window opens, locate the GAIN supported application you wish to uninstall in the list of installed programs, click on that entry one time, and then click on the "Add/Remove" or "Change/Remove" button (depending on which version of Windows you are using).</li>
	<li>Follow the on screen instructions.</li> 
</ol>
<p>In a very few cases, you may see an icon in the "Add/Remove Programs" section for GAIN software, but not individual software components. In this case, remove each of the GAIN-supported software applications as above, then remove the GAIN software as well.</p> 
<h4>Have more questions?</h4>
<p>Read our <a href="gain-faq.html">Frequently Asked Questions section</a> to find answers to questions people have asked about uninstalling GAIN software from their computer.</p>
<h4>Contacting Claria</h4>
<p>Claria has set up an <a href="gain-hotline.html">Uninstall Hotline</a>, a <a href="gain-faxback.html">Faxback service</a>, as well as continued <a href="mailto:support@gainpublishing.com ">email support</a> to assist you in uninstallation.  You can find these services and more on our <a href="support.html">Support page</a>.</p>
<h4>GAIN-Supported Software Privacy Policy</h4>
<p><a href="http://www.gainpublishing.com/global/help/privacy_statement.html">GAIN-Supported Software Privacy Policy</a></p>
<br/>

